Hey, i'm working on an embedded C++ project for an automotive ECU and i've run into a really annoying issue. The system has a gradual RAM exhaustion that only shows up after about 4-5 hours of continuous operation. I've checked the main loops but everything looks okay. Here is a snippet of the telemetry processing class where i suspect something might be going on:

```cpp
class TelemetryProcessor {
private:
    std::vector<uint8_t>* buffer;
    size_t bufferSize;

public:
    TelemetryProcessor(size_t initialSize) : bufferSize(initialSize) {
        buffer = new uint8_t[bufferSize];
    }

    void processPacket(const uint8_t* data, size_t len) {
        if (len > bufferSize) {
            // Attempting to resize if packet is too large
            delete[] buffer;
            bufferSize += len; 
            buffer = new uint8_t[bufferSize];
        }
        std::memcpy(buffer, data, len);
    }

    ~TelemetryProcessor() {
        delete[] buffer;
    }
};
```

Can you give me a systematic way to track down where exactly the leak is happening? It's hard to catch with standard tools because of the real-time constraints on the hardware.

